From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:33:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 440/488] [DS4.1] Token log-softmax in TileLang

compute_token_logprobs ran Triton's _topk_log_softmax_kernel: each row's
max and log-sum-exp over the vocabulary, then the requested tokens'
logprobs. The TileLang kernel is its contract bit for bit, with the
arithmetic read from the cached Triton 3.7 kernels' PTX and SASS on the
nodes (16-byte-aligned layouts: FP32 4 + 4 elements a thread 512 apart,
BF16 8 consecutive; exponentials in register order, warp XOR 16..1,
warps as (w0 + w2) + (w1 + w3), blocks in order; non-FTZ ex2.approx and
__nv_logf; no FMA). register_topk_scores_warmup declares it; the Triton
kernel stays as the tests' reference.
